{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"The error sweep exposed a real FFI bug: `pcre2_get_error_message_8(INT_MIN, ...)` aborts because translated Rust uses checked unary negation, while the compiled C wraps and returns `\"no error\"`. I’m changing that single operation to `wrapping_neg()`, which reproduces the observed C result without altering other error numbers."}}
